WEBVTT

00:02:28.504 --> 00:02:30.866
because I always know
it's going to be good.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:33.318
CA: Well, I can't imagine
what you've been through

00:02:33.342 --> 00:02:34.759
these past couple years,

00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:36.459
but let's perhaps not start there.

00:02:36.483 --> 00:02:40.230
Why don't we start with
the subject of your TED Talk

00:02:40.254 --> 00:02:42.372
and the subject of "Big Magic,"

00:02:42.396 --> 00:02:46.170
which is that these insights
that you have around creativity,

00:02:46.194 --> 00:02:50.461
they are not the usual story
we hear about creativity.

00:02:50.485 --> 00:02:55.184
In the TED Talk, you put out there
this notion that creative genius

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.846
wasn't something that people have.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:00.638
It's not like there are ordinary people
and then there are these geniuses